      "id": "AspNet.AssetManager",
      "range": "*"
    },
    "message": "Renamed to AspNet.AssetManager in v3.0.0, which also supports Vite since v4.0.0. Install AspNet.AssetManager instead. The namespace changed to AspNet.AssetManager, AddAspNetWebpack() to AddAssetManager(), and bundle names now include the view folder (Views_Home_Index instead of Home_Index). v4.0.0 also renamed the Webpack configuration section to AssetManager. The release notes for v3.0.0 and v4.0.0 list every breaking change: https://github.com/Baune8D/AspNet.AssetManager/releases",
    "reasons": [
      "Legacy"
    ]
  },
